course: dictionary
lesson: 252
title: Alpine: words about high mountains
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you exactly where something is. Alpine means to do with high mountains, especially the Alps in Europe. «Alpine meadows» are grassy fields high up a mountain, and an «alpine village» is a village in the mountains.
explain: Look at the words around alpine to check its meaning. «Alpine marmots are big ground squirrels that whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes.» Marmots live high on mountains, so alpine tells you which kind of marmot this is. Ask yourself: what kind of place or thing is it?
explain: Alpine can also be a noun. An alpine is a small plant that grows high on mountains. In sport, «alpine skiing» means racing down slopes, which is different from cross-country skiing. The same word can describe in one sentence and name something in another, so always check the sentence.
fact: Alpine means to do with high mountains, especially the Alps in Europe.
fact: «Alpine marmots» are big ground squirrels that whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes.
fact: Alpine marmots hibernate for about six months, and they sleep in family groups.
fact: «Alpine ibex» climb almost vertical stone walls, like the Cingino dam in Italy, to lick salt.
fact: In sport, «alpine skiing» is racing downhill, as opposed to cross-country skiing.
exercise: «Alpine marmots whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes.» What does alpine tell you? | They are very fast runners | They like to live by the sea | They are kept in a zoo | *They live high on mountains, in the Alps
exercise: What is «alpine skiing»? | Skiing across flat fields for miles | Swimming in a cold lake | *Racing down slopes | Climbing up a tall tree
exercise: What does «alpine meadow» mean? | A dark forest in a valley | *A grassy field high up a mountain | A flat field beside the sea | A river that runs under the ground
test: Gardeners grow alpines in rock gardens. What is an alpine? | *A small plant that grows high on mountains | A tool for digging stones | A kind of cake made with nuts | A large animal that lives in the sea
test: Which place is most likely to be called alpine? | *A high mountain meadow above the trees | A dry desert with no plants | A sandy beach by the sea | A busy city street at night
exam: «Alpine ibex» climb walls to lick salt from the stones. What does alpine mean here? | *Belonging to high mountains, like the Alps | Belonging to a farm | Belonging to a busy city | Belonging to the sea
